  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Indonesia Partnership for Justice (Phase 3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through AIPJ3, the Australian Government works in partnership with the Indonesian Government to support its priority law and justice reforms. This program will advance the long-term goal of establishing strong and accessible justice and security institutions to uphold the rule of law and contribute to stability and prosperity. AIPJ3 focuses on seven priority areas: accountability and transparency, criminal justice reform, preventing violent extremism, transnational crime cooperation, commercial law, access to justice, and women&#x2019;s leadership. AIPJ3 will foster connections between Australian and Indonesian government agencies, civil society organisations, universities and the private sector &#x2013; deepening existing partnerships and building new linkages. It aims to develop innovative solutions and strategies to tackle law, justice and security challenges in Indonesia and the region.</narrative>
  </description>
